{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Application Software vs System Software "}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "A1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about application and system software."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understands systems theories, business processes and basic concepts on IT.  Create a map of processes that allows identifying areas in an information system, using IT tools to generate reports based on the company's needs."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level.  Recognizes basic ideas on IT concepts, systems theory, and diagrams of processes."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Connectors"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Connectors</span> are words that form different relationships between words and clauses. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Connectors</span> give equal emphasis to the two clauses they connect. They are known as conjunctions. The connectors help you to organize what you say in a more logical form. <br/><br/> The most common simple connector are <span class=\"strong\">but, and, nor, yet</span> and <span class=\"strong\">or</span>.  <br/> One of the most common connector to make contrast is <span class=\"strong\">but</span>. It is a connector that joins two independents ideas. They have a subject and a verb. They are commonly followed by a comma. <br/><br/> Examples:<br/> <li><span class=\"italic\">This application software is not for John, but Mark. </span></li><br/> <li><span class=\"italic\">We're going to buy a computer, but we're also going to buy a printer. </span></li>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Yes, you did, but let me explain"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you need to do a sum up you can do it with this utility, but if you need to do a more specialized task then you need to upload application software on the computer."}, {"type": "example", "content": "We learned that software is categorized into application software and system software."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Application Software and System Software"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Computer software</span> can be classified into types based on common function. These are two general classifications: <span class=\"strong\">application software</span> and <span class=\"strong\">system software</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": " <span class=\"strong\">Software</span> performs special functions like basic operation of the computer and entertainment functions. There are many different types of systems and applications software because the range of tasks that can be performed with a computer are big. <br/><br/> Classification: <br/><br/> 1. <span class=\"strong\">Application software</span> refers to the computer system. They are the productivity programs because they enable the user to complete a task. For example, you may use the <span class=\"italic\">Word</span> processor to write  a letter. </br></br> 2. <span class=\"strong\">System software</span> refers to the computer hardware and other platforms. These programs are dedicated to manage the computer. For example, the operating system that your computer has like <span class=\"italic\">Windows</span> or <span class=\"italic\">Linux</span>."}, {"type": "example", "content": "System software can include device drivers, operating systems, utilities and malware. For example: when you turn on your computer the operating system allows hardware devices to talk to each other, it can control the way they work."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "malware"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an application software or program design to damage a system"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: System software can include device drivers, operating systems, utilities, and malware."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob03aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "turn on "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to start a machine by pushing or pulling a bottom"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: When you turn on your computer the operating system allows hardware devices to talk to each other, it can control the way they work."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob03aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "allow "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to permit something by giving permission"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: When you turn on your computer the operating system allows hardware devices to talk to each other, it can control the way they work."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob03aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "run "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to execute a program or instruction"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: An application software refers to the computer system and special functions, but system software refers to the computer hardware and other platforms to run application software."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le02ob03aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "cont